{"page": 10, "kind": "cell", "table": 1, "row": 14, "col": 3, "x": null, "text": "Content Standard SS.4.8.17.2 Analyze major events that led to the unification of Hawaiʻi Island by Kamehameha I", "id": "u252", "furniture": false}
{"page": 10, "kind": "cell", "table": 1, "row": 14, "col": 4, "x": null, "text": "• Major Events: the three prophecies (born under a bright star on a stormy night, lifting the Naha stone, building of Pu‘ukoholā Heiau), the gaining of mana by Kamehameha I (inheritance of the Kū image from Kalani‘ōpu‘u, recognition as an outstanding warrior, marriage to higher ranking wives), battle victories (Mokuʻohai, Hilo, Kaʻu)", "id": "u253", "furniture": false}
